  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPVO &#x2013; Improving the livelihoods of workers in the granite slabs surfaces supply chain from India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a collaboration between Arte Groep and Stichting Local Impact Hub from the Netherlands and AARKS Stonex India and Paradigm Shift from India. It focuses on the granite quarries in Khammam, and the factory in Ongole, South India. The location of the quarries are in Telangana Province. The beneficiaries of this project are the workers in the quarries and factories in the granite supply chain.The project focuses at identifying the working risks and labour rights risks, in order to mitigate these risks and diminish them in phase B. In the quarries the risks are higher, also since there are quite a lot of migrant workers, and contracted workers in the quarries. Living wage is the second relevant sustainability issue. The minimum wage in India is set by the government, and all companies are upheld to this wage. Often quarry workers are hired through a contractor. Investigation will be made of types of contract forms in quarries and factory and the income strategies of the workers&apos; families, in order to assess how and where income improvements towards living income can be made. In phase B the project will focus on activities and interventions on the risks that are most prominent from the risk assessment.</narrative>
  </description>
